A||||5||BroCar 87||HELP!!!! I lost my starter bolts. How do I replace them?||||9||
Z||000000||BroCar 87||11-12-2000||11:12 PM||||Hey guys, back in June I took out my starter of my 84 to place it in my 87 (both 4 cylinder coupes). Now I am putting a brand new starter back in the 84. BUT I lost the bolts. How do replace the bolts with new ones. I know they were two different sizes, so can I buy them from the auto parts store? I asked them and they said try the junk yard or a dealer. <BR>Went to the junk yard and couldn't reach a foot under the cars. Haven't called the dealer yet due to them being closed on the weekends.<BR>Anyone know the sizes of these bolts I am looking for???<BR>Thanks for ANY info on this  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature2.jpg">  <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>   Custom dual side exit exhaust!||||reg||9
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||11-12-2000||11:24 PM||||Try going to a 'REAL' parts store, they can help.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ur2biteme||11-13-2000||05:24 AM||||had the same problem a few months ago.  went to kragen, checked them all out, bought bolts, left, put them on the starter.  i hate wrecking yards.  some ignorant moron trying to tell me that this 87 coupe was an 84 SE when i was looking for a fuel line that seemed to be specific 87-88 (also happened to have a DIS brick on the engine and the proper '87 body), and then trying to charge me $55 for it!  i even showed him the date stamped in the door pannel.  i said F that and used some garden hose to patch the line for a couple days.  worked like a charm.  i'll try to avoid junk yards at all costs unless i'm refered to some place specifically.  besides, these A**h**es are so damn lazy!  o.k. i'll stop now.<P>------------------<BR>UR2BITEME<BR>'87 econo coupe<BR>170k and a bad fender :(||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||11-13-2000||05:22 PM||||I had the same thing with mine about a month or so ago except I lost the starter bolt somewhere on the way to work.<P>I think they are 10mm x 1.5's,  Use the starter case to get the correct lengths.  Try to aim for about 3/4" to 1" of thread engagement.<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tigger||11-13-2000||05:34 PM||||LoL.. be sure to use the blue thread lock.||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||11-13-2000||07:39 PM||||The GM starter bolts only come in a couple lenghts far as I know. The only real choice is metric or SAE thread that I can remember.<P>You want the actual starter bolt not a generic replacement if you can avoid it. The starter bolts are made to resist falling out. (Not that they are really good at it.)||||reg||1
